        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The largest angle is opposite 7 cm. Its cosine is $-\\frac12$, so it is $120^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "The largest angle $\\theta$ is opposite the longest side, 7 cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{5^2+3^2-7^2}{2(5)(3)}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{-15}{30}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac12\\\\\\theta&=120^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the exact area of the triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{15\\sqrt3}{4}\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "worked": "The $120^\\circ$ angle lies between the sides of lengths 5 cm and 3 cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(5)(3)\\sin120^\\circ\\\\A&=\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{15\\sqrt3}{4}\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
